        "original_id": "ae617280-a779-5943-b0f7-019b000762c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aimé Césaire, William Shakespeare, Jean-Marie Serreau\n- Works: Une Tempête, Discours sur le colonialisme, The Tempest\n- Places: Martinique, Tunisia, Hammamet\n- Events: Festival d'Hammamet\n- Roles: poet, author, politician\n\nFacts:\n- Aimé Césaire was born on 26 June 1913 and died on 17 April 2008.\n- Aimé Césaire was a Francophone and French poet, author, and politician from Martinique.\n- Aimé Césaire wrote Discours sur le colonialisme, an essay about the strife between colonizers and the colonized.\n- In 1969, Aimé Césaire wrote Une Tempête.\n- Une Tempête was written as a response to William Shakespeare's play The Tempest.\n- Une Tempête was first performed at the Festival d'Hammamet in Tunisia under the direction of Jean-Marie Serreau.",
